; A finite local-confluence diamond for compatible beta reduction. This is evidence about the
; encoding, not a proof of Church-Rosser: the general theorem requires induction and a transitive
; closure (or parallel reduction) at the meta level.
load lambda

; Reducing the root first.
(app (λ x x) (app (λ y y) unit)) ↦ (app (λ y y) unit)
(app (λ y y) unit) ↦ unit

; Reducing the argument first reaches a different intermediate term.
(app (λ y y) unit) ↦ unit
(app (λ x x) (app (λ y y) unit)) ↦ (app (λ x x) unit)
(app (λ x x) unit) ↦ unit
